{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379494-vampiric-supernatural-hunters","id":1379494,"title":"Vampiric supernatural hunters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-08T10:48:00-07:00","id":1379494,"title":"Vampiric supernatural hunters?","content":"So Inquisition implies supernatural hunters (aka. hunters who is supernatural himself), just like Vampire Hunter D or Hellsing, do exist but very rare. <br /> *So I think about a supernatural hunter who is VAMPIRE himself*<br /> <br /> And to be honest I don\u2019t find any canon npcs except Beckett\u2019s childer and those in original The Hunters Hunted<br /> <br /> So do you know more about this in canon? Have you created or played them for while? What\u2019s your idea about them? To be honest I even suspect some supernaturals may be in Second Inquisition!<br /> <br /> TIP: Edict it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-08-2020, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T11:49:36-07:00","id":1379505,"title":"","content":"There was the Demon Hunter X book. Been forever since I looked at it, so I don't recall if it had any in canon characters. It does seem like the early editions had encouraged mortals with psychic numina to be antagonists/NPCs, but they kind of fell by the wayside over time.<br /> <br /> I suppose there could be some Celestial Chorus or surviving Knights Templar that take the vampire hunting thing seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T15:43:42-07:00","id":1379533,"title":"","content":"Numinous mortals (people with psychic and hedge magic powers) exist in the Arcanum book.<br /> The Society of Leopold wields True Faith, which is a supernatural capability. <br /> Demon Hunter X talked about dhampris.<br /> Rogue ghouls are a thing that has existed for a long time.<br /> <br /> You'd have to do some searching through related material, but they're there, and the Arcanum has a number of named cnaon NPCs that exist across books and editions..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T19:24:25-07:00","id":1379578,"title":"","content":"Sorry but I mean vampires who become supernatural hunter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T03:37:12-07:00","id":1379723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379494-vampiric-supernatural-hunters?p=1379578#post1379578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry but I mean vampires who become supernatural hunter</div> </div> </div> </div>that would be the tal'mahe'ra and the Inconnu","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T04:21:30-07:00","id":1379727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379494-vampiric-supernatural-hunters?p=1379723#post1379723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that would be the tal'mahe'ra and the Inconnu</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall badass like Alucard, which may be a methseulah in WoD, and hunt evil beings with righteousness (?)... romantic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T04:56:47-07:00","id":1379731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379494-vampiric-supernatural-hunters?p=1379727#post1379727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall badass like Alucard, which may be a methseulah in WoD, and hunt evil beings with righteousness (?)... romantic</div> </div> </div> </div>Alucard wouldn't work in VtM,<br /> a powerful Vampire serving humans would be...ugh<br /> <br /> even mechanically that wouldn't work with the beast and humanity and...all that shtick<br /> <br /> but there are ways to bypass it, you can have synthetic vampires created by the Technocracy (projenitors) or stuff like that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:11:16-07:00","id":1379792,"title":"","content":"A Salubri may be suitable... passably <br /> <br /> The theme of VtM limits this kind of fairy tale strictly, a vampire hunter who is righteous may be just a pawn of greater being","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:23:41-07:00","id":1379797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379494-vampiric-supernatural-hunters?p=1379533#post1379533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Numinous mortals (people with psychic and hedge magic powers) exist in the Arcanum book.<br /> The Society of Leopold wields True Faith, which is a supernatural capability.<br /> Demon Hunter X talked about dhampris.<br /> Rogue ghouls are a thing that has existed for a long time.<br /> <br /> You'd have to do some searching through related material, but they're there, and the Arcanum has a number of named cnaon NPCs that exist across books and editions..</div> </div> </div> </div>What Demon Hunter X said about dhampyr hunters was &quot;not with these groups!&quot;, though a bit later, there was a book dedicated to dhampyrs, hunters or otherwise. Naturally, it had a dhampyr who joined the shih, because WW had to WW. A V20 take would probably have relaxed the restrictions from DHX, just as W20 stopped being uptight about some of its potential but forbidden character options, but since it involves KotE, nothing has become of it.<br /> <br /> Edit: In the meantime, though, Half-Damned makes having high Humanity an asset of sorts for a dhampyr that hunts monsters, as it can be used to get a skill-boosting power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T13:40:42-07:00","id":1382232,"title":"","content":"In Chicago By Night there was the Nosferatu vampire Nathaniel who hunted other vampires. He hated all his kind.<br /> <br /> You already mentioned The Hunters Hunted; of course the original book described the Children of Osiris and while not stated outright, there is a strong implication they hunted and destroyed the Followers of Set.<br /> <br /> And of course the Red List of the Camarilla is a list of vampires specifically targeted for destruction by other vampires. And the various Blood Hunts of individual Princes of course. Not everyone targeted by that is simply a political dissident, but outright danger. And any vampires who are succumbing to the Beast, entering Wassail, etc. will also be hunted and destroyed even if they don't have those specific statuses.<br /> <br /> So there's lots of vampires who specifically hunt and destroy other vampires for a variety of reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T12:15:41-07:00","id":1382365,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall a vampire who hunted other vampires in order to commit diablerie on them but justified his addiction to diablerie as &quot;taking out monsters.&quot; Can't remember if that was an official character or one somebody made and posted on the forums years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T12:04:04-07:00","id":1382567,"title":"","content":"Any of the Banu Haqim have the potential to be the supernatural hunter that you are looking for. Older members can pretty much track anybody down, at any given time. It may take them a few days, or longer if their prey is smart enough to avoid them. Assassin/Hunter/Diablerist/Hound all titles that can easily be applied to the Banu(Assamites)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26038-feargrounds","name":"FearGrounds","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T16:57:48-07:00","id":1382637,"title":"","content":"Because Vampire was the first game line in the World of Darkness, vampires get the short end of the stick against other supernaturals due to the incredible power creep that set in as each subsequent game was released. Even the Sabbat Inquisition and False Hand stick to assaulting other vampires.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you're statting the supernatural antagonists strictly as Vampire game line characters instead of doing a crossover chronicle, all bets are off. Heck, even a single Brujah like Nines Rodriguez could take down a lupine one on one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 04-19-2020, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T03:49:25-07:00","id":1382942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379494-vampiric-supernatural-hunters#post1379494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Inquisition implies supernatural hunters (aka. hunters who is supernatural himself), just like Vampire Hunter D or Hellsing, do exist but very rare. <br /> *So I think about a supernatural hunter who is VAMPIRE himself*<br /> <br /> And to be honest I don\u2019t find any canon npcs except Beckett\u2019s childer and those in original The Hunters Hunted<br /> <br /> So do you know more about this in canon? Have you created or played them for while? What\u2019s your idea about them? To be honest I even suspect some supernaturals may be in Second Inquisition!<br /> <br /> TIP: Edict it</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I feel there would be a lot more Vampires who want to go all Blade and Genocide the Kindred. My first character which was in a game that fizzled I was planning to have him go autarkis and from there want to eliminate all Kindred. I mean vampires are numerous and literally thrive off of stealing and manipulating exclusively, besides the vegans that only eat animal blood, leave them maybe.<br /> <br /> This is why the Path of Blood and Path of Mayaparitsatya (spelling?) make sense to me, they want to bring order to the world, and handle the situation of the Kindred not following rules and having a harmonious place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T03:51:26-07:00","id":1382943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379494-vampiric-supernatural-hunters?p=1382637#post1382637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Vampire was the first game line in the World of Darkness, vampires get the short end of the stick against other supernaturals due to the incredible power creep that set in as each subsequent game was released. Even the Sabbat Inquisition and False Hand stick to assaulting other vampires.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you're statting the supernatural antagonists strictly as Vampire game line characters instead of doing a crossover chronicle, all bets are off. Heck, even a single Brujah like Nines Rodriguez could take down a lupine one on one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dubious on the Lupine slaying... come on everyone knows those Ron Spencer art scenes where one Lupine is massacring a whole Sabbat Pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T04:59:35-07:00","id":1382955,"title":"","content":"Where the Lupine has one guy's entire head in its mouth? God, I love that picture.<br /> <br /> It shows the tragedy of the Sabbat in a nutshell. These people have been granted immortality, and they squander it doing dumb shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 04-21-2020, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T05:45:42-07:00","id":1384172,"title":"","content":"Ferox leaps to mind as a vampire who hunted other vampires. He is or was a Gargoyle with True Faith. Nosferatu were his prey of choice. He thought they were demons due to their mishapen appearance. More deluded than sane. He was, however a hero of the Gargoyles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T06:46:22-07:00","id":1384181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379494-vampiric-supernatural-hunters?p=1384172#post1384172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ferox leaps to mind as a vampire who hunted other vampires. He is or was a Gargoyle with True Faith. Nosferatu were his prey of choice. He thought they were demons due to their mishapen appearance. More deluded than sane. He was, however a hero of the Gargoyles.</div> </div> </div> </div>no, Ferox was a joke character for Revised edition, just like Sam Haight for 2nd edition<br /> <br /> they're a parody of munchkin min/max player characters<br /> <br /> Sam Haight was a character that mixed different splats, he was a werewolf ghoul with magick etc (which was possible in 2nd ed, and toned down in revised)<br /> <br /> Ferox was a powerful gargoyle with wings who cheated the game by having max True Faith and unbondable merit (True Faith being one of the op plot devices easily accessible to player characters)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T19:47:59-07:00","id":1385177,"title":"","content":"Now now, Ferox only had True Faith 9. It was that hot young dhamphir who God spoke to from her maxi pads in the first Gehenna scenario who maxed out her True Faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T21:13:03-07:00","id":1385182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379494-vampiric-supernatural-hunters?p=1382955#post1382955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where the Lupine has one guy's entire head in its mouth? God, I love that picture.<br /> <br /> It shows the tragedy of the Sabbat in a nutshell. These people have been granted immortality, and they squander it doing dumb shit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its only more honest about it. Most camarilla Neonates die. Most ANarch Neonates die. They don't get immortality hell they probably don't get to outlive if they'd had a normal human life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T09:08:48-07:00","id":1385250,"title":"","content":"Alastors are vampire hunters. Josians are vampire hunters. They mostly hunt other vampires, but I think there's no dearth of vampire hunters in the WoD...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T13:07:15-07:00","id":1385288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379494-vampiric-supernatural-hunters?p=1384181#post1384181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> no, Ferox was a joke character for Revised edition, just like Sam Haight for 2nd edition<br /> <br /> they're a parody of munchkin min/max player characters<br /> <br /> Sam Haight was a character that mixed different splats, he was a werewolf ghoul with magick etc (which was possible in 2nd ed, and toned down in revised)<br /> <br /> Ferox was a powerful gargoyle with wings who cheated the game by having max True Faith and unbondable merit (True Faith being one of the op plot devices easily accessible to player characters)</div> </div> </div> </div>Haight didn't start out that way. He was supposed to be a Garou adversary, and then things started getting far out of hand. He died by the time 2e was fairly new, though; The Chaos Factor was his last stand, and came out about the same time that Mage and Werewolf were just getting their 2nd editions, so it'd be more accurate to say that he was a creation of first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T14:03:06-07:00","id":1385300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379494-vampiric-supernatural-hunters?p=1385288#post1385288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haight didn't start out that way. He was supposed to be a Garou adversary, and then things started getting far out of hand. He died by the time 2e was fairly new, though; The Chaos Factor was his last stand, and came out about the same time that Mage and Werewolf were just getting their 2nd editions, so it'd be more accurate to say that he was a creation of first edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>oh, I see, my bad","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T14:42:11-07:00","id":1385302,"title":"","content":"Defo Nathaniel Bordruff from CbN 5e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T05:34:00-07:00","id":1458656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379494-vampiric-supernatural-hunters?p=1384181#post1384181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> no, Ferox was a joke character for Revised edition, just like Sam Haight for 2nd edition</div> </div> </div> </div>Ferox first appeared in <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/The_Kindred_Most_Wanted_(book)\" target=\"_blank\">Kindred Most Wanted</a>, definitely a 2nd edition book since it came in '94, about 4 years before <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_Revised_Edition\" target=\"_blank\">Revised</a> edition's debut.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379494-vampiric-supernatural-hunters?p=1384181#post1384181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they're a parody of munchkin min/max player characters<br /> <br /> Sam Haight was a character that mixed different splats, he was a werewolf ghoul with magick etc (which was possible in 2nd ed, and toned down in revised)<br /> <br /> Ferox was a powerful gargoyle with wings who cheated the game by having max True Faith and unbondable merit (True Faith being one of the op plot devices easily accessible to player characters)</div> </div> </div> </div>He was also one of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boudica\" target=\"_blank\">Boudica</a>'s unamed children with Prasutagus and a 1000+ years old ghoul who survived through the change of multiple masters who, disturbed by his new Tremere's bosses treatment of their creations, would partly inspire the Gargoyles uprising against their creators - a role that would be pretty much taken by Virstania from VtDA/DA:V onwards - before being embraced. Bonus irony, if Virstania exists in one's game Ferox would <b>never </b>have been embraced as Gargoyle, since that happened pretty much because they didn't know they could keep him alive &amp; unaging as a ghoul with <b>their </b>vitae.<br /> <br /> So in my games Ferox is &quot;just&quot; Virstania's ghoul lieutenant/kindred lore guide/pet sexy MacLeod-expy with Fabio hair. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-04-2021, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T10:35:30-07:00","id":1458689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379494-vampiric-supernatural-hunters?p=1379792#post1379792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Salubri may be suitable... passably</div> </div> </div> </div>Curiously my Kindred character that I played the most was <i><u>precisely</u></i> a Salubri vampire hunter.<br /> <br /> She was also the character I started with less confidence that she would survive, being actually in a Changing Breeds chronicle. I just wanted to see if I could make a vampire character survive a week in that game.<br /> <br /> It was a Gen 8 basic Salubri with Humanity 9 and True Faith in Gaia, as she was a Silent Strider Kinfolk in life. When the Uktena of the pack witnessed her holding against a Mage with True Faith invoking the names of Gaia and some totems he decided to take her a pet of sorts.<br /> <br /> Although I'm personally in favor of players doing that kind of shit themselves if they want, the ST was even more insane than us and I ended up with the Phoenix as personal totem...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}